# /etc/conf.d/gt-be98-macaddr - Runner port MAC overrides (gt-be98-macaddr)
# Written by the web UI; saved to /jffs (gt-be98-save, ALLOW_PATHS of
# /etc/conf.d/gt-be98-jffs). Keys here win over /etc/conf.d/gt-be98-drivers.
# Empty = the default: rnr0 the factory MAC from the DT, the other ports the
# board's base MAC made locally administered, +N for rnrN.
#   RNR_MAC_BASE=aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff  base for every port (locally administered, +N)
#   RNR_MAC<N>=aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff    exactly this MAC for rnrN (unicast)
# Apply without a reload: gt-be98-macaddr --apply [rnrN]
